        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Mapper layer follows the established pattern.** `formatRiskFlag` sits alongside `formatPossibleDuplicate`, `formatCapacityWarning`, `formatDeleted`, etc. \u2014 same null-owner guard, same thin delegation to an `Owner` method, same javadoc style. The `@Mapping` wiring matches the surrounding expression-mapped fields exactly.\n\n- **Business logic lives in the model, not the mapper.** `riskFlag()` is a composing method that reads like the existing derived accessors, and it delegates to primitives rather than inlining the rules.\n\n- **New email logic is placed with its peers and reuses the right primitives.** `isDisposableAdjacentEmailDomain` sits directly after `isDisposableEmailDomain`, shares `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS`, and factors the common label extraction into `registrableBase` (a `private static` helper) rather than duplicating parsing \u2014 a good split, not a catch-all.\n\n- **No duplication introduced**, and neither `Owner` nor `OwnerMapper` is becoming a grab-bag \u2014 each addition is parallel to what's already there.\n\n- **OpenAPI schema addition** mirrors the other `readOnly` boolean derived fields in shape and placement.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find all of this natural."
